  "placement": "Book page 226, topic 8.5.1 গোলীয় উত্তল আয়নায় প্রতিবিম্ব: next to চিত্র ৮.১৯ (a pencil XY in front of a convex mirror, its image X′Y′ smaller); also 8.8.2 (page 235, the rear-view mirror).",
  "order": 1,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "cm",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for the image in a convex mirror, book pages 225–227 and 235, topics 8.5.1 and 8.8.2, next to চিত্র ৮.১৯. The book's pencil XY stands before a convex mirror (f = 15 cm) on an optical bench with a printed cm scale. The pencil is seen in the silver by an exact traced reflection, small and upright. The book's three rays are traced on the exact sphere one at a time; their extensions meet behind the mirror at X′, where the virtual image grows. The student drags the pencil from 4 to 75 cm with live u, v and m; the image stays upright and smaller, between P and F, sliding along the one line it cannot leave. Last, from one eye, the same mirror plane and then convex shows why a rear-view mirror is convex. Five test questions on the picture. Offline, Bangla and English.",
  "tags": [
    "light",
    "reflection",
    "spherical mirror",
    "convex mirror",
    "virtual image",
    "mirror formula",
    "rear-view mirror",
    "optical bench",
    "bangla"
  ],
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "lang",
      "label": "Language",
      "type": "select",
      "options": [["bn", "বাংলা"], ["en", "English"]],
